{"title":"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 58","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><i>The following problem is from the Ultimate Question of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest\" title=\"2007 iTest\">2007 iTest</a>, where solving this problem required the answer of a previous problem.  When the problem is rewritten, the T-value is substituted.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_58&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For natural numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/4/f24c5767fd4a3d4b1cf770981fe45377fcf61f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k,n\\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" />, we define\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/7/a47d32ef7dbe4b05db19a8a472f8633b2db03705.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S(k,n)=\\left\\lfloor\\frac{2^{n+1}+1}{2^{n-1}+1}\\right\\rfloor+\\left\\lfloor\\frac{3^{n+1}+1}{3^{n-1}+1}\\right\\rfloor+\\cdots+\\left\\lfloor\\frac{k^{n+1}+1}{k^{n-1}+1}\\right\\rfloor\\]\" width=\"437\" height=\"43\" />\nCompute the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/2/f9215ddb0a76d20e6c4def31c95719f71c691cbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(10,112)-S(10,55)+S(10,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"255\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_58&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/a/76ab31665e6b46042c0753ded91b4cb6f9a588c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(k,n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> can be rewritten as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/e/deeaeedab308bc9afa27a8446c90dbb808f22201.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{j=2}^{k} \\left\\lfloor\\frac{j^{n+1}+1}{j^{n-1}+1}\\right\\rfloor\\]\" width=\"114\" height=\"52\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/2/352ac36bdd967223f3574a3782bcb61ff0b368be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = j^{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />.  With the substitution, each similar part becomes\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d7d491e12f58f079236c3eee575bdc3b537c45.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{j=2}^{k} \\left\\lfloor\\frac{j^2 \\cdot x+1}{x+1}\\right\\rfloor\\]\" width=\"119\" height=\"52\" />\nPerforming polynomial division results in\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/2/0c2cfed9325bcb65c05d57593ebbf7ff2fe34703.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{j=2}^{k} \\left\\lfloor j^2 + \\frac{1 - j^2}{x+1}\\right\\rfloor\\]\" width=\"134\" height=\"52\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/6/2f6c353a0d35407c6674fd1b71f3382e69d48b5e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{j=2}^{k} \\left\\lfloor j^2 - \\frac{j^2 - 1}{j^{n-1}+1}\\right\\rfloor\\]\" width=\"153\" height=\"52\" />\nWhen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/4/33447feb72186a11c702bea5ca681081d37d6750.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 112$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/1/f0126a8af0c273138c6f6903efb72142ab6722ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 55$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/f/60f74be8645b423cbb32ff7a7a64bb3ffbffb31b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{j^2 - 1}{j^{n-1}+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"68\" height=\"42\" /> is close to zero, which means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/0/ad088d352cda03d36adbb1584295a99a52b8ac33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor j^2 - \\frac{j^2 - 1}{j^{n-1}+1}\\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"131\" height=\"45\" /> would be the same for a given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/4/33447feb72186a11c702bea5ca681081d37d6750.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 112$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/1/f0126a8af0c273138c6f6903efb72142ab6722ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 55$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/f/19ffdcfe941d05e55ae2e10e334de4bf5086b352.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(10,112) - S(10,55) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"205\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nThat means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/1/c51360347a059ad64f13f92e14708fa65d59f1b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(10,112) - S(10,55) + S(10,2) = S(10,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"341\" height=\"18\" />, and that equals\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a894f81b4fbc10c45b1a2341e405cc1e6200906.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{j=2}^{10} \\left\\lfloor j^2 - \\frac{j^2 - 1}{j+1}\\right\\rfloor\\]\" width=\"134\" height=\"52\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/6/3b62f744cb34b5a8560576e99efbdeada53020b7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{j=2}^{10} \\left\\lfloor j^2 - (j-1) \\right\\rfloor\\]\" width=\"133\" height=\"52\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/7/2171809d0bee9bb7e7aad200cd8c534a729e1be7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{j=2}^{10} j^2 - \\sum_{j=2}^{10} (j-1)\\]\" width=\"144\" height=\"52\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/9/13951ba642d99df0d39d46b370bef28d93b22814.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(4+9 \\cdots 100) - (1+2 \\cdots 9)\\]\" width=\"219\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bd1e80d0aa608bab7f75a57a52e0c110ae6a3bb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\frac{10 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 21}{6} - 1) - (\\frac{10 \\cdot 9}{2})\\]\" width=\"208\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e736e48e77c731bfea578b80912f3c5257631054.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[384-45\\]\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/d/37dea0cbda481dd73573abe9c7d2d0f425dab4b1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{339}\\]\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_58&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest\" title=\"2007 iTest\">2007 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 iTest Answer Key\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_57\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 57\">Problem 57</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_59\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 59\">Problem 59</a></b>\